<title>USA: Abrams Industries Inc Q4 shr $0.72 vs $.07.</title>
<headline>Abrams Industries Inc Q4 shr $0.72 vs $.07.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourth quarter ended		 4/30/97	    4/30/96</p>
<p> Revenues				  43,719,673	31,433,604</p>
<p> Earnings before income taxes	 3,411,306	   321,286</p>
<p> Income tax expense (benefit)	 1,291,000	   124,000</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss)		    2,120,306	   197,286</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss) per share		.72		 .07</p>
<p> Weighted avg shrs outstanding	2,950,634	 2,970,856</p>
<p>    Twelve months ended		    4/30/97	 4/30/96</p>
<p> Revenues				  $136,123,601  $134,299,240</p>
<p> Earnings before income taxes	   3,848,398     (467,188)</p>
<p> Income tax expense (benefit)	   1,457,000     (163,000)</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss)			2,391,398     (304,188)</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss) per share		  .81	   (.10)</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding  2,965,800     2,977,163</p>
<p>NOTES: The company said all segments were profitable in 1997, with the manufacturing division showing a substantial turn-around because of its &quot;re-engineering efforts.&quot;</p>
<p>The company reported its backlog of contracts for the next 12 months rose to $61.2 million at end of Q4 1997 from $36.1 million a year ago.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
